{"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene\/defaultLaunchBehavior(_:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","text":"MainActor","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultLaunchBehavior","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"behavior","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SceneLaunchBehavior","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/SceneLaunchBehavior","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI19SceneLaunchBehaviorV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene","text":"Scene","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP"},{"text":"\n","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This behavior can be used to define if a scene is shown on application"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"launch in the absence of any previously saved state."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"On platforms that do not support multiple windows, this value is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ignored.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On platforms other than Windows, there must be at least one scene that"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"presents itself. If no scenes are defined to present, the first scene","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"will be presented, regardless of the value provided to this modifier."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"During app launch, on platforms other than Windows, the system","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"will only consider scenes whose role matches the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/bundleresources\/information_property_list\/uiapplicationpreferreddefaultscenesessionrole"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key in the application scene manifest of the "},{"code":"Info.plist","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" file.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"For instance, a volumetric window would need the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIWindowSceneSessionRoleVolumetricApplication"},{"type":"text","text":" role."}]}],"name":"Note","type":"aside","style":"note"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On Windows, this behavior will also be used to determine which scene is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"presented when clicking on the icon of a running application with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"visible windows."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On visionOS, the system may background the last dismissed scene instead"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of closing it. Thus, the suppressed behavior additionally specifies that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the scene should not be presented when tapping on the application icon"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with no visible windows."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For example, you may wish to present a welcome window on launch of your"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app when there are no previous document windows being restored:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["@main","struct MyApp: App {","    var body: some Scene {","        DocumentGroup(newDocument: MyDocument()) { configuration in","            DocumentEditor(configuration.$document)","        }","","        Window(\"Welcome to My App\", id: \"welcome\") {","            WelcomeView()","        }","        .defaultLaunchBehavior(.presented)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default value for all scenes if you do not apply this modifier is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/SceneLaunchBehavior\/automatic","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". With that strategy, a scene"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"will only present itself if it is the first scene defined by the app,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and no other scenes have presented themselves."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultLaunchBehavior","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"SceneLaunchBehavior","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI19SceneLaunchBehaviorV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Scene","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP"}],"title":"defaultLaunchBehavior(_:)","extendedModule":"OpenSwiftUI","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5ScenePAAE21defaultLaunchBehavioryQrAA0dfG0VF","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Sets the default launch behavior for this scene.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/scene\/defaultlaunchbehavior(_:)"]}],"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/SceneLaunchBehavior/automatic":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The automatic behavior."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/scenelaunchbehavior\/automatic","title":"automatic","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"automatic","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI19SceneLaunchBehaviorV","text":"SceneLaunchBehavior","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/SceneLaunchBehavior\/automatic"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/Scene":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Scene"}],"title":"Scene","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/scene","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Scene"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A part of an app’s user interface with a life cycle managed by the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system.","type":"text"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/SceneLaunchBehavior":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SceneLaunchBehavior","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The launch behavior for a scene."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/scenelaunchbehavior","title":"SceneLaunchBehavior","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SceneLaunchBehavior","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/SceneLaunchBehavior"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/Scene/defaultLaunchBehavior(_:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"te